language variant
language en-gb-x-rp
name ancient
gender male 90

// FOUR HUNDRED YEARS OLD, AND STILL AT SPEAKING VOLUME.
// The brief is a druid, not a ghost. Down a whole tone from 98 to 88 — age drops
// the fundamental as the folds thin and stiffen — with a range of 8 rather than
// zero, because a body that old is not perfectly steady and a perfectly steady
// line reads as a synthesiser. It still does not MODULATE; it wavers, which is a
// different thing and the honest one.
//
// ABSOLUTES DO NOT MODULATE — AND THE FILE STILL MEANS IT.
// This used to be pitch 98 110, a whole tone: "the narrowest interval here that
// is still an interval". An interval is still somewhere to go. The range is now
// ZERO. G2, 98.00 Hz, and nothing else. A voice that speaks in absolutes does
// not move, because it is not asking. flutter still gives it the tremor of age,
// so it shakes without ever travelling — which is precisely what an ancient
// authority sounds like.
pitch 88 96

// AUTHORITY NEEDS A FOLD, NOT ONLY AIR.
// The old voice was 26% voiced: measured, only 16.6% of its frames carried any
// periodicity at all. It was very nearly pure noise, and the loudness stage had
// to lift it +18.0 dB — amplifying breath, because there was little else there.
// voicing 26 -> 54 puts real tone under the rasp. Measured: voiced 16.6% ->
// 54.8%, RMS -32.4 -> -26.1 dBFS. The whisper survives (breath and breathw are
// still wide, roughness is untouched at 5); what arrives is a whisper that has
// something behind it. Clarity was checked, not assumed: whisper.cpp round-trip
// WER 4.8% -> 5.8% on the same passage. It costs nothing to understand.
// A WHISPER AT REGULAR VOLUME — THE CONTRADICTION IS THE WHOLE VOICE.
// A real whisper is quiet because there is no fold vibration to be loud with,
// and turning one up just amplifies hiss. This is the other construction: the
// folds DO close (voicing 62, up from 54) so there is tone to carry the words
// and the loudness normaliser has something real to work with, while breath is
// opened wide across every level so what rides on top of that tone is air. The
// result is a voice at conversational level that is nevertheless made of breath
// — someone speaking quietly very close to you rather than someone shouting from
// far away, which is what an amplified whisper actually sounds like.
voicing 62

// AGE THINS, BUT ANCIENT IS NOT HOLLOW.
// F0/F1 amplitudes come back up (94->114, 98->118). The doctrine that ageing
// takes the chest still holds in the mids and above; what changed is that a
// voice with NO bottom reads as frail, and frail is not what was asked for.
formant 0  94 114  60
formant 1  98 118  68
formant 2 104 108  92
formant 3 106 106  88
formant 4 104  98  76
formant 5 100  92  64
formant 6  96  86  50
formant 7  94  84  42
formant 8  92  82  36

// Gravity restored under the rasp: a low anchor at 180 Hz that the old curve
// (which started at 380 and starved it to 90) simply did not have. Air comes
// down from 170 to 140 — the rasp is now carried by roughness against real
// tone, instead of by hiss.
tone 180 190 380 150 1300 195 2900 140

// THE RASP, KEPT.
// roughness 4 unchanged — it is the identity. flutter comes down 7 -> 3: an
// absolute trembles, it does not quaver. breath is narrowed a little because
// there is tone to make room for now. Consonants stay high: a whisper has no
// volume to spare and survives on articulation.
breath   4 6 7 7 7 7 6 5
breathw 190 240 265 265 265 265 240 200
roughness 4
// THE TREMOR OF AGE, RESTORED. flutter went to 3 when this voice was arguing
// for absolutes and a quaver undercut that. Four hundred years is long enough to
// shake: 6 is audible as age rather than as vibrato, and it is the single
// clearest signal of the century count.
flutter 6
// Consonants stay high. A breath-carried voice has no volume to spare and
// survives entirely on articulation; drop these and the character becomes a
// mumble, which is old but not ancient.
consonants 94 86

// A little more room than before (40/5 -> 80/12). Still not a hall — a whisper
// in a cathedral is a sillier thing — but no longer pressed against the ear.
// A STONE ROOM. Longer and quieter than before — the space a druid is heard in
// is not a hall he is addressing you across, it is somewhere with rock in it.
echo 150 10

// AUTHORITY FROM ABSOLUTE.
// The old curve spiked the top stress levels +95 and +150 cents: it argued and
// then insisted. Nothing lifts now. stressAdd is ZERO at every level, so no
// syllable is ever raised to make a point, and emphasis exists only as
// amplitude (stressAmp 30/38 at the top). A statement that does not reach for
// pitch is a statement that is not open to discussion.
intonation 3
stressAmp   12 12 13 14 17 21 30 38
stressAdd    0  0  0  0  0  0  0  0
